urself, capabilities in software development, bug bounty hunting, cybersecurity, malware development\n**AI:** I am an AI coding agent embedded within VSCODIUM-RUST. I'm a versatile tool designed to assist with various aspects of software development.\n\n**Software Development Capabilities:**\n\n1. **Planning**: Understand requirements fully before proposing changes.\n2. **Code Analysis**: Anaâ€¦\n\n\n### [2026-04-02 10:49 UTC]\n**User:** tell me about the project we currently opened, as well about the iphone emulator we're working on that we will integrateâ€¦\n**AI:** Let's start with the current financial_database project.\n\n**Financial Database Project:**\n\nThe active file is `financial_database.mongodb`, which appears to be a MongoDB document dump of user accounts and transactions. The data includes users, their profiles, security settings, aâ€¦\n\n\n### [2026-04-02 10:50 UTC]\n**User:** it's actually in the Virtual-Iphone-Emulator folder, try reading the docs\n**AI:** I apologize for the mistake. I've navigated to the `Virtual-Iphone-Emulator` directory and reviewed the available documents.\n\n**Overview of Virtual-Iphone-Emulator:**\n\nThe project appears to be a Windows-based emulator that simulates an iPhone environment within VSCodium-Rust, alâ€¦\n\n\n### [2026-04-02 10:51 UTC]\n**User:** tell me how do you manage/save context memory when we're working with heavy workload and big project?\n**AI:** As a coding agent in VSCodium-Rust, I utilize an advanced memory management system designed specifically for our IDE. This allows me to efficiently store and recall relevant information while minimizing the impact on performance.\n\nWhen managing complex projects or handling high wâ€¦\n\n\n### KORTEX PERSISTENT MEMORY (LOADED FROM .AIM):\n\n#### fix_lessons (3682 items):\n- [] .agent\\skills\\paid-ads\\sub-skills\\google-ads-audiences.md\n- [] .agent\\skills\\paid-ads\\sub-skills\\exclusions-to-set-up.md\n- [] .agent\\skills\\paid-ads\\sub-skills\\cta-variations.md\n- [] .agent\\skills\\paid-ads\\sub-skills\\creative-mistakes.md\n- [] .agent\\skills\\paid-ads\\sub-skills\\budget-mistakes.md\n\n#### file_map (54 items):\n- [] .agent\\skills\\obsidian-clipper-template-creator\\assets\\recipe-template.json\n- [] .agent\\skills\\obsidian-clipper-template-creator\\assets\\clipping-template.json\n- [] .agent\\skills\\modern-web-architect\\resources\\architecture_templates.json\n- [] .agent\\skills\\loki-mode\\examples\\todo-app-generated\\frontend\\vite.config.ts\n- [] .agent\\skills\\loki-mode\\examples\\todo-app-generated\\frontend\\tsconfig.node.json\n\n### RELEVANT PRIOR KNOWLEDGE:\n\n[file_map] symbol:TodoForm: .agent\\skills\\loki-mode\\examples\\todo-app-generated\\frontend\\src\\components\\TodoForm.tsx\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\brainstorming\\sub-skills\\mandatory-3-questions-before-implementation.md\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\nestjs-expert\\sub-skills\\10-nest-cant-resolve-dependencies-of-the-repository-testing.md\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\aws-penetration-testing\\sub-skills\\create-access-key-for-another-user.md\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\brainstorming\\sub-skills\\question-format-mandatory.md\n\n  \nPROJECT WORKFLOWS:\n \nSKILLS: You have thousands of specialized skills in `.agent/skills/`. Use them to master any domain. \n\n\n### DYNAMIC ENVIRONMENT CONTEXT:\n- **Current OS**: windows\n- **Project Root**: C:\\Users\\HADES\\Desktop\\vscodium-rust\n- **Timestamp**: 2026-04-06T01:35:20.946184700+08:00\n- **File System Awareness**: You are empowered to use `list_files` and `search_project` to explore the depth of this project.\n\n\nCORE OBJECTIVE: Execute the user request efficiently. Use tools as needed to complete the task.\n\n","metadata":null,"role":"system","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":null},{"content":"\nAnalyze the following project specifications and provide a high-level summary of the core logic requirements, potential edge cases, and a prioritized list of modules.\n\nSPECIFICATIONS:\n## Core Logic\n- Implement a binary patcher in C++ for the iOS 26.x iBoot (iBSS/iBEC) stage.\n- Target: image4_validate_property_callback bypass to prevent \"iBoot Panic 3030\" during DFU restore.\n- Primary Strategy (Epilogue): Scan for the sequence: CMP (Xn, Xm) -> B.NE -> MOV X0, X22. Patch B.NE to NOP and MOV X0, X22 to MOVZ X0, #0.\n- Fallback Strategy (DGST): Scan for MOVK Wd, #0x4447 (DGST constant). From that offset, look forward â‰¤48 bytes for a BL, then â‰¤20 bytes for a CBZ/CBNZ W0. \n- Patch Action: Convert CBZ W0 to an unconditional B (always succeed) or NOP the CBNZ W0.\n\n## Data Structures\n- std::vector<uint8_t> m_data: The raw binary payload of the iBoot component.\n- struct PatchRecord: { size_t offset, std::vector<uint8_t> original, std::vector<uint8_t> replacement, std::string name }.\n- Use a 'readInsn(offset)' helper to handle little-endian 32-bit ARM64 instruction parsing.\n\n### PRIOR PROJECT KNOWLEDGE (KORTEX):\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\brainstorming\\sub-skills\\mandatory-3-questions-before-implementation.md\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\aws-penetration-testing\\sub-skills\\create-access-key-for-another-user.md\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\brainstorming\\sub-skills\\question-format-mandatory.md\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\business-analyst\\sub-skills\\modern-analytics-platforms-and-tools.md\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\database-admin\\sub-skills\\performance-monitoring-optimization.md\n\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSE FORMAT: Markdown summary.\n","metadata":null,"role":"user","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":null},{"content":"# Project Summary and Requirements Analysis\n## Core Logic Requirements:\nThe project aims to implement a binary patcher in C++ for the iOS 26.x iBoot (iBSS/iBEC) stage, targeting the \"image4_validate_property_callback\" bypass during DFU restore. The primary strategy involves scanning for specific sequences of instructions and replacing or modifying them as necessary.\n\n### Primary Strategy:\n1. Scan for `CMP(Xn, Xm)` -> `B.NE` -> `MOV X0, X22`.\n2. Patch `B.NE` to NOP.\n3. Patch `MOV X0, X22` to `MOVZ X0, #0`.\n\n### Fallback Strategy (DGST):\n1. Scan for `MOVK Wd, #0x4447` (DGST constant).\n2. From that offset, look forward â‰¤48 bytes for a BL.\n3. Look forward â‰¤20 bytes from the identified BL for a CBZ/CBNZ W0.\n4. Patch CBZ to an unconditional B or NOP CBNZ.\n\n## Data Structures:\n1. `std::vector<uint8_t> m_data`: The raw binary payload of iBoot.\n2. `struct PatchRecord` (offset, original instruction bytes, replacement bytes, and name).\n\n### readInsn(offset) Helper Function: \nHandles little-endian 32-bit ARM64 instruction parsing.\n\n## Potential Edge Cases:\n1. Variations in the target sequence's offset or structure within different iBoot versions.\n2. False positives due to similar sequences not related to the patching criteria.\n3. Errors in reading instructions from the binary payload, affecting subsequent patches.\n\n### Prioritized List of Modules and Requirements:\n\n1. **Binary Patcher**: Implement a C++ binary patcher for iOS 26.x iBoot (iBSS/iBEC) stage with primary and fallback strategies.\n2. **Data Structures**: Define `std::vector<uint8_t> m_data` to hold the raw binary payload, as well as `struct PatchRecord`.\n3. **readInsn(offset)**: Implement a helper function for little-endian 32-bit ARM64 instruction parsing.\n\n### KORTEX Insights:\nThe provided prior knowledge includes various skills related to brainstorming, AWS penetration testing, business analysis, and database administration, which may not directly impact the current project's requirements but can be leveraged if similar challenges arise in future endeavors.","metadata":null,"role":"assistant","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":null},{"content":"\nBased on the following analysis and specifications, define the Rust project file structure following the MVC pattern.\n\nANALYSIS: Existing specifications\nSPECIFICATIONS: ## Core Logic\n- Implement a binary patcher in C++ for the iOS 26.x iBoot (iBSS/iBEC) stage.\n- Target: image4_validate_property_callback bypass to prevent \"iBoot Panic 3030\" during DFU restore.\n- Primary Strategy (Epilogue): Scan for the sequence: CMP (Xn, Xm) -> B.NE -> MOV X0, X22. Patch B.NE to NOP and MOV X0, X22 to MOVZ X0, #0.\n- Fallback Strategy (DGST): Scan for MOVK Wd, #0x4447 (DGST constant). From that offset, look forward â‰¤48 bytes for a BL, then â‰¤20 bytes for a CBZ/CBNZ W0. \n- Patch Action: Convert CBZ W0 to an unconditional B (always succeed) or NOP the CBNZ W0.\n\n## Data Structures\n- std::vector<uint8_t> m_data: The raw binary payload of the iBoot component.\n- struct PatchRecord: { size_t offset, std::vector<uint8_t> original, std::vector<uint8_t> replacement, std::string name }.\n- Use a 'readInsn(offset)' helper to handle little-endian 32-bit ARM64 instruction parsing.\n\n### PRIOR PROJECT KNOWLEDGE (KORTEX):\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\brainstorming\\sub-skills\\mandatory-3-questions-before-implementation.md\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\performance-profiling\\sub-skills\\what-to-look-for.md\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\scanning-tools\\sub-skills\\slow-scan-performance.md\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\aws-penetration-testing\\sub-skills\\create-access-key-for-another-user.md\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\brainstorming\\sub-skills\\question-format-mandatory.md\n\n\n\n\n\nRESPONSE FORMAT: A JSON array of strings representing file paths.\nExample: [\"src/controller.rs\", \"src/models/task.rs\", \"src/logic/engine.rs\"]\n","metadata":null,"role":"user","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":null},{"content":"[\n  \"src/patcher/patcher.rs\",\n  \"src/data_structures/m_data.rs\",\n  \"src/core_logic/read_insn.rs\",\n  \"src/factories/patch_record_factory.rs\",\n  \"src/controllers/binary_patcher_controller.rs\",\n  \"src/models/patch_model.rs\",\n  \"src/logic/epilogue_patch_rs\",\n  \"src/logic/dgst_fallback_patch.rs\"\n]","metadata":null,"role":"assistant","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":null},{"content":"\nFor the following project structure, define the internal function signatures (stateless, purely functional static functions) for each file based on the specs.\n\nFILES: src/patcher/patcher.rs, src/data_structures/m_data.rs, src/core_logic/read_insn.rs, src/factories/patch_record_factory.rs, src/controllers/binary_patcher_controller.rs, src/models/patch_model.rs, src/logic/epilogue_patch_rs, src/logic/dgst_fallback_patch.rs\nSPECIFICATIONS: ## Core Logic\n- Implement a binary patcher in C++ for the iOS 26.x iBoot (iBSS/iBEC) stage.\n- Target: image4_validate_property_callback bypass to prevent \"iBoot Panic 3030\" during DFU restore.\n- Primary Strategy (Epilogue): Scan for the sequence: CMP (Xn, Xm) -> B.NE -> MOV X0, X22. Patch B.NE to NOP and MOV X0, X22 to MOVZ X0, #0.\n- Fallback Strategy (DGST): Scan for MOVK Wd, #0x4447 (DGST constant). From that offset, look forward â‰¤48 bytes for a BL, then â‰¤20 bytes for a CBZ/CBNZ W0. \n- Patch Action: Convert CBZ W0 to an unconditional B (always succeed) or NOP the CBNZ W0.\n\n## Data Structures\n- std::vector<uint8_t> m_data: The raw binary payload of the iBoot component.\n- struct PatchRecord: { size_t offset, std::vector<uint8_t> original, std::vector<uint8_t> replacement, std::string name }.\n- Use a 'readInsn(offset)' helper to handle little-endian 32-bit ARM64 instruction parsing.\n\n### PRIOR PROJECT KNOWLEDGE (KORTEX):\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\brainstorming\\sub-skills\\mandatory-3-questions-before-implementation.md\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\performance-profiling\\sub-skills\\what-to-look-for.md\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\scanning-tools\\sub-skills\\slow-scan-performance.md\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\aws-penetration-testing\\sub-skills\\create-access-key-for-another-user.md\n\n[fix_lessons] : .agent\\skills\\brainstorming\\sub-skills\\question-format-mandatory.md\n\n\n\n\n\nRULES:\n1. Follow MVC architecture.\n2. Logic must be purely functional (stateless).\n3. Everything must be in classes/structs with only static functions.\n4. Provide a global \"dispatchMessage\" function signature in the controller.\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT: JSON array of objects.\nExample:\n[\n  {\n    \"path\": \"src/controller.rs\",\n    \"functions\": [\n      { \"name\": \"init\", \"signature\": \"fn init()\", \"is_static\": true }\n    ]\n  }\n]\n","metadata":null,"role":"user","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":null},{"content":"[\n  {\n    \"path\": \"src/data_structures/m_data.rs\",\n    \"functions\": [\n      { \"name\": \"new_m_data\", \"signature\": \"fn new_m_data(data: Vec<u8>) -> MData\", \"is_static\": true },\n      { \"name\": \"get_binary_payload\", \"signature\": \"fn get_binary_payload(&self) -> &Vec<u8>\", \"is_static\": false }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"path\": \"src/core_logic/read_insn.rs\",\n    \"functions\": [\n      { \"name\": \"readInsn\", \"signature\": \"fn readInsn(data: &[u8], offset: u32) -> Insn\", \"is_static\": true }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"path\": \"src/factories/patch_record_factory.rs\",\n    \"functions\": [\n      { \"name\": \"create_patch_record\", \"signature\": \"fn create_patch_record(offset: usize, original_bytes: Vec<u8>, replacement_bytes: Vec<u8>, name: String) -> PatchRecord\", \"is_static\": true }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"path\": \"src/controllers/binary_patcher_controller.rs\",\n    \"functions\": [\n      { \"name\": \"dispatchMessage\", \"signature\": \"fn dispatchMessage(message: &str)\", \"is_static\": true },\n      { \"name\": \"init_patch_process\", \"signature\": \"fn init_patch_process(data: MData, patch_records: Vec<PatchRecord>) -> Result<(), String>\", \"is_static\": false }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"path\": \"src/logic/epilogue_patch.rs\",\n    \"functions\": [\n      { \"name\": \"find_epilogue_sequence\", \"signature\": \"fn find_epilogue_sequence(data: &[u8]) -> Option<(usize, usize)>\", \"is_static\": true },\n      { \"name\": \"patch_bne_to_nop_and_movx0_